libcamera: sensor: Add OV02E10 static properties and sensor delays

The OV02E10 has no entry in the sensor properties database, so libcamera
warns "No sensor delays found in static properties" and assumes a gain
delay of 1 frame. Intel's IPU7 camera HAL config for this sensor
(ov02e10-uf.json) uses exposureLag 2 and gainLag 2. With the wrong gain
delay, AGC misreads which gain each frame was taken with, which can make
it overshoot at start-up. With the delays set, brightness settles by frame 3.

Unit cell size: 1.12 um (OmniVision OV02E product brief).

For the OV02E10 on the Galaxy Book5 Pro (940XHA), against libcamera v0.8.0.
build-patched-libcamera.sh applies it on 0.8.0 full installs (step 4e).

diff --git a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
index 20cfd0b..c2d9b60 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -376,6 +376,16 @@ const CameraSensorProperties *CameraSensorProperties::get(const std::string &sen
 				.hblankDelay = 3
 			},
 		} },
+		{ "ov02e10", {
+			.unitCellSize = { 1120, 1120 },
+			.testPatternModes = {},
+			.sensorDelays = {
+				.exposureDelay = 2,
+				.gainDelay = 2,
+				.vblankDelay = 2,
+				.hblankDelay = 2
+			},
+		} },
 		{ "ov08d10", {
 			.unitCellSize = { 1120, 1120 },
 			.testPatternModes =  {
